# Design System Hard Rules

These rules are always-on and must never be violated.

## Styling

- **Tailwind CSS only** — no CSS modules, no styled-components, no inline `style={{}}` (GSAP inline transforms are the only exception)
- **Sizing units (use deliberately)**  
  - **Typography** — always `rem` (e.g. `text-lg`, arbitrary `text-[1.125rem]`).  
  - **Margins / padding on text blocks** — `rem` so rhythm scales with root type.  
  - **Borders / icon boxes** — `px` (hairlines and Lucide boxes: `border`, `w-[16px]`, `h-[16px]`, etc.).  
  - **Component chrome (buttons, chips, inputs)** — `em` for **internal** padding so it scales with that component’s `font-size` (see `Button` sizes).  
  - **Layout** — `%`, `vw`, or viewport height **`dvh` / `svh` / `lvh`** as appropriate; never bare **`vh`**, and never **`h-screen`** / **`min-h-screen`** (they map to classic viewport height behavior).
- **Viewport height** — pick **`dvh`**, **`svh`**, or **`lvh`** only:  
  - **`dvh`** — heroes and “fill the visible screen” sections (`min-h-dvh`, `min-h-[100dvh]`, fractional `dvh` for sticky stacks).  
  - **`svh`** — full-viewport **fixed** UI (mobile menu overlays, bottom bars, modals) so content stays in the safe zone when browser chrome is expanded.  
  - **`lvh`** — full-bleed **background** image/video layers so media covers the largest viewport without tracking every toolbar pixel.  
- **No hardcoded color values** — use CSS variables (`text-primary`, `bg-accent`, etc.) or Tailwind theme classes; never hardcode hex values like `#2E4036`
- **No semi-transparent section design** — sections must feel complete through either high-quality real paragraphs/prose or solid coloured elements/surfaces. Do not use translucent panels, glassmorphism, faded overlays, or section backgrounds like `bg-*/5`, `bg-*/10`, `backdrop-blur`, `opacity-*`, or `via-transparent` as the visual idea.
- **clsx + tailwind-merge** — always use the `cn()` utility for conditional classes; never string concatenation

## Components

- **Components first** — check `src/components/` before creating any new component
- **SectionWrapper always** — use `SectionWrapper` for all section padding; never add raw padding to `<section>` elements
- **Semantic HTML** — use `<button>` not `<div onClick>`; use `<section>` not `<div>` for page sections
- **Sharp images, rounded UI** — photography, media, and image wrappers are always rectangular with sharp corners (`rounded-none`). Rounding belongs to UI features only: buttons, chips, cards, accordions, form controls, badges, and other interactive/component chrome may use the approved radius tokens.

## Animation

- **GSAP for animation** — use the `useGSAP` hook with a cleanup context; no Framer Motion; no CSS keyframes for major animations

## Next.js

- **App Router only** — no `useRouter` from `next/router`; use `next/navigation`; use `<Link>` from `next/link`, not `<a>` for internal navigation

## TypeScript

- **Strict types** — no `any` types; all component props must be typed with interfaces or type aliases

## Dependencies

- **No new dependencies without asking** — the stack is locked: Next.js, Tailwind CSS, GSAP, Lucide, clsx, tailwind-merge

## Brand

- Read `.cursor/skills/brand-consistency/SKILL.md` before any design work
- Fonts: The Seasons (`font-display`), Outfit (`font-sans`), Cormorant Garamond (`font-serif`), Plus Jakarta Sans (`font-jakarta`), Jost (`font-jost`) — no substitutions
- Never use: Inter, Roboto, Arial, Space Grotesk, or system fonts
- **Feature sections** — item titles: `text-xl font-semibold md:text-2xl` + `font-display`; item body: `text-base` + `font-sans` + `text-foreground/75`. Import `featureItemTitleClass` / `featureItemBodyClass` from `src/lib/typography-classes.ts`. FAQ questions use `faqQuestionClass`.

## Composition & visual language

These are owner preferences — apply on every new section, card grid, or page block unless there is a strong reason not to.

- **Extraordinarily simple layout** — default to a plain, obvious structure: single column or a clean grid, generous whitespace, no clever asymmetry unless the section truly needs it. Prefer easy **vertical stacking** (icon → title → body) inside cards over side-by-side complexity. Reference: `PrivateEventsOccasions` occasion cards (`flex flex-col gap-5`, content in one column).
- **Style icons** — use the solid **foreground square + white Lucide icon** treatment for feature/occasion cards: `h-[44px] w-[44px] rounded-none bg-foreground text-on-dark` with a single Lucide icon at `h-[20px] w-[20px]` and `strokeWidth={1.75}`. One icon per item; icon sits above the title in the stack.
- **Coral title emphasis (critical)** — in section headings and hero titles, wrap **only the 2–3 most important words** in `HandDrawnUnderline` with `underlineClassName="text-accent"` (coral / brand accent). Do not underline whole lines or more than a short phrase. Vary `variant={1|2|3}` across sections. Never substitute a flat CSS `underline` or a different color for this pattern.
- **One elevating thread** — the base layout stays minimal; add **one** continuous, intentional, or animated detail that lifts the section (GSAP scroll reveal, draw-on underline, subtle stagger, pinned scroll moment, etc.). Avoid piling multiple competing effects on the same block.

## Visual Verification with Puppeteer (mandatory)

After **any** UI change or new page creation, take a Puppeteer screenshot before marking work done. Puppeteer is installed (`node_modules/puppeteer`).

Write to `/tmp/ss.mjs` and run `node /tmp/ss.mjs`:
```js
import puppeteer from "puppeteer";
const b = await puppeteer.launch({ headless: true });
const p = await b.newPage();
await p.setViewport({ width: 1440, height: 900 });
await p.goto("http://localhost:3000/YOUR_ROUTE", { waitUntil: "networkidle2", timeout: 10000 });
await p.screenshot({ path: "/tmp/ss.png" });
await b.close();
```
Open `/tmp/ss.png` and inspect it. Fix any visual issues before finishing.

- Screenshot the specific route you changed
- Test desktop (1440×900) and mobile (375×812) for new pages
- Dev server runs at `http://localhost:3000`
